export default {"X000108":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A simple algebra with a noninvertible nonzero matrix</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000792\"><span>Nonzero associative algebra</span><code>P000792</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000787\"><span>Finite-dimensional associative algebra</span><code>P000787</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000791\"><span>Central algebra over a field</span><code>P000791</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000790\"><span>Simplicity of an associative algebra</span><code>P000790</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000801\"><span>Finite central simple algebra</span><code>P000801</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000794\"><span>Positive square dimension</span><code>P000794</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000805\"><span>Matrix algebra over a finite central division algebra</span><code>P000805</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000108\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000108</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000788\"><span>Division algebra</span><code>P000788</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Unital associative algebras over a specified field</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Over any field <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_2(k)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> has only the two trivial two-sided ideals and center <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, whereas <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_{11}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is nonzero, has rank one and has no inverse.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/074D\">Stacks 074D · numbered source and proof</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/brauer/#tag-074D\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000108\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000108\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000109":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A finite simple real algebra with larger center</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000787\"><span>Finite-dimensional associative algebra</span><code>P000787</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000792\"><span>Nonzero associative algebra</span><code>P000792</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000790\"><span>Simplicity of an associative algebra</span><code>P000790</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000788\"><span>Division algebra</span><code>P000788</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000109\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000109</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000791\"><span>Central algebra over a field</span><code>P000791</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000801\"><span>Finite central simple algebra</span><code>P000801</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000794\"><span>Positive square dimension</span><code>P000794</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Unital associative algebras over a specified field</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> The real algebra <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is a field with center <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and has real dimension two.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/074A\">Stacks 074A · numbered source and proof</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/brauer/#tag-074A\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000109\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000109\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000110":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>Boundary case for the simple-module existence statement</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000787\"><span>Finite-dimensional associative algebra</span><code>P000787</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000791\"><span>Central algebra over a field</span><code>P000791</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000790\"><span>Simplicity of an associative algebra</span><code>P000790</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000110\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000110</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000792\"><span>Nonzero associative algebra</span><code>P000792</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000801\"><span>Finite central simple algebra</span><code>P000801</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000788\"><span>Division algebra</span><code>P000788</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Unital associative algebras over a specified field</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> If zero unital algebras are permitted, the zero algebra has exactly one two-sided ideal, dimension zero, and center equal to the image of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. Every unital module over it is zero. This explains the nonzero assumption in clause (1) of the source.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0746\">Stacks 0746 · numbered source and proof</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/brauer/#tag-0746\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000110\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000110\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000126":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A flat local completion with unchanged residue field and nonreduced target</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000625\"><span>Local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings</span><code>P000625</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000208\"><span>Flat ring map</span><code>P000208</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P001007\"><span>Source maximal ideal generates the target maximal ideal</span><code>P001007</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P001008\"><span>Finite separable residue extension of a local map</span><code>P001008</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P001025\"><span>Ring homomorphism with reduced source</span><code>P001025</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000126\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000126</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000372\"><span>Essentially finite type ring map</span><code>P000372</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P001009\"><span>Étale local homomorphism in the Noetherian convention</span><code>P001009</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P001026\"><span>Ring homomorphism with reduced target</span><code>P001026</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Ring homomorphisms</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Ferrand and Raynaud give a one-dimensional Noetherian local domain whose maximal-ideal completion has a nonzero square-zero ideal. Its completion map is flat, generates the target maximal ideal and induces an isomorphism on residue fields. Essential finite type would make this an étale local homomorphism, contradicting ascent of reducedness in Tag 025O.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/039U\">Stacks 039U · numbered source and proof · Stacks 039U · failure of reducedness on dropping essential finite type</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/etale/#tag-039U\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.numdam.org/item/ASENS_1970_4_3_3_295_0.pdf\">D. Ferrand and M. Raynaud, Fibres formelles d’un anneau local noethérien, Proposition 3.1, r=1</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02JD\">Stacks 02JD · explicit characteristic-zero construction</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/examples/#tag-02JD\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/025O\">Stacks 025O · reducedness for étale local homomorphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/etale/#tag-025O\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000126\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000126\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000100":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A finite étale cyclotomic algebra with unit Vandermonde differences</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000231\"><span>Étale ring map</span><code>P000231</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000203\"><span>Finite ring map</span><code>P000203</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000100\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000100</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000211\"><span>Surjective ring map</span><code>P000211</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Ring homomorphisms</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Take <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝐙</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R=\\mathbf Z[1/p]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> for a prime <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\ge3</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S=R[X]/(\\Phi_p)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. The monic degree <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> presentation makes <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> free of rank at least two, so <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R\\to S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is not surjective. In <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the factorization of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T^p-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> into linear terms has unit derivative at every root, so the differences between distinct roots are units. The monic presentation therefore also has invertible derivative, giving a finite étale <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-algebra.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03GF\">Stacks 03GF · numbered source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-03GF\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000100\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000100\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000101":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A completion at an infinitely generated maximal ideal that fails completeness</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000080\"><span>Local ring</span><code>P000080</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000101\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000101</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000122\"><span>Complete local ring</span><code>P000122</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Commutative rings</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Localize <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X_1,X_2,\\ldots]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> at the ideal generated by all variables, and take its completion there. The resulting ring is local. Its maximal ideal strictly contains the extension of the original maximal ideal, and the ring fails completeness for its own maximal ideal, as shown by the completion calculation in Stacks 05JC.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JC\">Stacks 05JC · numbered source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/examples/#tag-05JC\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0324\">Stacks 0324 · numbered source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0324\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000101\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000101\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000102":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A finitely presented quotient with non-quasi-compact smooth locus</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000211\"><span>Surjective ring map</span><code>P000211</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000202\"><span>Ring map of finite presentation</span><code>P000202</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000102\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000102</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000746\"><span>Quasi-compact smooth locus of a ring map</span><code>P000746</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Ring homomorphisms</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Take <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R=k[x,y_1,y_2,\\ldots]/(xy_i:i\\ge1)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> over a field and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=R/(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. The map is an isomorphism on each <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(y_i)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. At the remaining point, the origin in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec}(A)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the nonzero ideal generated by <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> prevents flatness of the local quotient. The opens <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(y_i)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> cover the smooth locus and no finite subfamily suffices, as may be seen by setting all but one <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y_i</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> equal to zero.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07CB\">Stacks 07CB · Numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/smoothing/#tag-07CB\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000102\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000102\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>"};
